          "independentVisualQA": "pending",
          "originalCaption": "Fig. 2: The OPTED pipeline. Large-scale pre-training produces the privileged teacher trained with RL in a render-free simulator on vectorized states (HD-map polylines and actor bounding boxes), subsequently adapted with further RL training to the distillation dataset. The end-to-end student is trained in open loop via behavior cloning on images recorded from human demonstrations, regressing its plan τ t \\tau_{t} onto the logged trajectory τ t GT \\tau_{t}^{\\mathrm{GT}} . OPTED fine-tuning then runs three steps iteratively. (1) The student drives the rendered simulator in closed loop: it receives frame o t o_{t} , predicts τ t \\tau_{t} , and the controller converts the plan into the action a t a_{t} that advances the simulator. (2) Each visited state is synchronized into the vectorized simulator, where the frozen teacher is stepped K K times to produce a trajectory of length | τ t | |\\tau_{t}| . (3) Student observations fill a bounded FIFO buffer of recent rollouts, and the student is trained on them with the imitation loss ℓ \\ell , KL for action heads or weighted L 1 \\mathrm{L}_{1} for waypoint heads (Eqs. 3 , 4 ).",
          "imageSourceURL": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.20756v1/fig_pipeline.png",
          "sha256": "93691aafceb2a861c9f29e4e05d0115c044f97e2811268edcf791d770b7dc71b",
